    ("Calculus", "partial derivative", "Holding the other inputs fixed isolates one coordinate's effect; collecting the partial derivatives for all inputs gives the gradient vector used to update every parameter."),
    ("Information Theory", "entropy of a distribution", "An unlikely outcome is more surprising and so carries more information; averaging the surprise -log p over the distribution gives the entropy, which is largest when the outcomes are most uncertain."),
